WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:04.570
Why are we forced to work?!

00:00:04.630 --> 00:00:07.890
Why must we pay money
in order to eat?!

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:09.950
Can't we all just share?

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:11.670
The rich get fat

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:13.600
while the poor die!

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:16.400
Where is the true freedom
in this world?!

00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:19.550
We are all slaves to our work!

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:21.570
And is work fun?

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:23.920
No! How could it be?!

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:26.850
We do not want to work, period!

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:30.510
That's why I, Hammerhead,
will change our society

00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:32.650
into one where only those
who want to work will work,

00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:35.070
while the rest are supported!

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:37.540
We will create a utopia!

00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:41.230
The Paradisers led by me, Hammerhead,
will make all this a reality!

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:48.450
Boss, no one's listening.

00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:49.510
What did you say?!

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:52.680
Bah! These civilians are idiots!

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:53.970
Let's go!

00:00:53.970 --> 00:00:57.860
Zeniru's the richest man in town.

00:00:57.860 --> 00:00:59.940
We'll wreck his posh penthouse
and show them we're serious!

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:02.620
High-rise apartments
are symbols of inequality!

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:03.880
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:18.000
One punch

00:01:21.710 --> 00:01:23.460
Three, two, one, kill shot

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:27.220
sanjou, hisshou, shijou saikyou

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:27.220
He joins the fight, he wins, the strongest in history

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:29.220
nan datten da, frustration

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:29.220
Are you talking to him? Frustration

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:30.720
ore wa tomaranai

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:30.720
He's not going to stop

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:34.850
one punch, kanryou, rensenrenshou

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:34.850
One punch, that's it, one fight after another

00:01:34.850 --> 00:01:38.480
ore wa katsu, tsune ni katsu, asshou

00:01:34.850 --> 00:01:38.480
He wins, he always wins, overwhelmingly

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:42.310
power, get power

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:42.310
Power, get power

00:01:42.310 --> 00:01:45.280
girigiri genkai made

00:01:42.310 --> 00:01:45.280
On to the very edge

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:46.490
Hero

00:01:46.490 --> 00:01:49.650
ore o tataeru koe ya

00:01:46.490 --> 00:01:49.650
There are voices praising him

00:01:49.650 --> 00:01:52.700
kassai nante hoshiku wa nai sa

00:01:49.650 --> 00:01:52.700
but he's not doing this for acclaim

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:53.950
Hero

00:01:53.950 --> 00:01:58.710
dakara hitoshirezu aku to tatakau

00:01:53.950 --> 00:01:58.710
So he just fight evil without end

00:01:58.710 --> 00:02:00.170
Nobody knows who he is

00:02:00.170 --> 00:02:04.340
sora ooi oshiyoseru teki

00:02:00.170 --> 00:02:04.340
Enemies to fight are numerous as the stars

00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:04.380
{OP Sync Point - Smiley Star, First Frame}

00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:07.420
ore wa se wo muke wa shinai

00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:07.420
and he's not gonna turn his back on you

00:02:07.420 --> 00:02:08.760
Hero

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:13.760
naraba yuruginaki kakugo shita tame

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:13.760
He's made up his mind and ain't gonna yield

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:20.980
tatakau hero

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:20.980
A fighting hero

00:02:20.980 --> 00:02:27.530
kodoku na hero

00:02:20.980 --> 00:02:27.530
A lone hero

00:02:23.150 --> 00:02:23.820
I

00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:24.480
I

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:25.110
I

00:02:25.110 --> 00:02:26.070
I

00:02:26.070 --> 00:02:26.740
I

00:02:26.740 --> 00:02:27.280
I

00:02:27.530 --> 00:02:32.530
i wanna be a saikyou hero

00:02:27.530 --> 00:02:32.530
I wanna be the strongest hero

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:42.720
This whole building is Zeniru's home.

00:02:43.910 --> 00:02:46.790
There's no way he made
so much money legally.

00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:49.140
Unforgivable! Bring it down!

00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:49.960
Yes, sir!

00:03:04.090 --> 00:03:06.010
Target has been destroyed!

00:03:06.820 --> 00:03:10.260
As expect from these powerful
experimental battle suits.{Hm, these experimental battle suits
sure pack a wallop.}

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:14.580
It was definitely worth risking
our lives to steal them.

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:16.900
Wait, that was the wrong building.

00:03:18.310 --> 00:03:19.520
My bad, Boss.

00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:21.640
Zeniru's house is a little further up.

00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:25.400
Everyone makes mistakes!

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:28.880
The important thing is to learn
from them. Am I right?

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:30.050
Yes, you're right!

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:32.940
All right, let's go to Zeniru's apartment.{All right, then onward to Zeniru's!}

00:03:46.610 --> 00:03:49.610
Thanks, bicycle guy!

00:04:10.780 --> 00:04:14.920
Don't come asking to play rock, paper, scissor
with a booger on your finger!

00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:19.410
A dream?

00:04:20.970 --> 00:04:23.100
The terrorist group responsible
for the riots

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:25.320
call themselves the Paradisers.

00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:27.740
They have destroyed
a high-rise building in City F.

00:04:27.820 --> 00:04:30.190
The situation seems to
be spiraling out of control.

00:04:30.990 --> 00:04:34.690
We have just learned
the identity of their leader.

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:40.700
m 0 0 l 500 0 500 110 0 110

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:40.700
B-CLASS CRIMINAL :
HAMMERHEAD

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:37.710
Hammerhead is a B-class criminal

00:04:37.870 --> 00:04:39.240
who has been involved in several

00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:40.700
violent incidents in the past.

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:43.680
He is a man of large stature,

00:04:43.810 --> 00:04:46.230
standing 2.15m tall
and weighing 210kg.

00:04:46.350 --> 00:04:47.390
According to one report,

00:04:47.390 --> 00:04:50.040
he once fought 20 men
in a street brawl

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:52.660
and sent them all to the hospital.

00:04:53.830 --> 00:04:57.500
The Paradisers sent the following
message to this TV station.

00:04:57.700 --> 00:04:59.640
"We will continue to riot until food,
clothing and shelter

00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:02.850
"are provided free of charge
to those who do not work,"

00:05:02.850 --> 00:05:05.680
- amongst other unintelligible demands.

00:05:03.260 --> 00:05:04.990
- Sounds pretty boring.

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:08.770
- Like Hammerhead, the group is
made up of unemployed young men

00:05:08.770 --> 00:05:12.150
- with no motivation to work.

00:05:08.900 --> 00:05:11.080
- No need for me to get involved.

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:15.990
- Also, the group members
all have shaven heads,

00:05:15.990 --> 00:05:18.950
making them quite intimidating.

00:05:18.950 --> 00:05:22.620
Those who encounter
any shaven-headed men on the street

00:05:22.620 --> 00:05:25.030
are advised to leave
the area immediately.

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:27.260
What the hell?

00:05:28.370 --> 00:05:29.180
But that's—

00:05:29.190 --> 00:05:30.080
They stole

00:05:30.170 --> 00:05:31.780
my look!

00:05:32.320 --> 00:05:33.840
I spend all this time
trying to be a hero,

00:05:34.340 --> 00:05:35.600
If they keep this up...{but if they keep acting
like this, I'll be treated}

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:36.410
Won't people start treating me

00:05:36.410 --> 00:05:37.890
like a villain?!

00:05:39.380 --> 00:05:41.250
I'm gonna smash them!

00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:43.610
Run!

00:05:43.680 --> 00:05:44.510
It's them!

00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:46.430
The Paradisers are coming.

00:05:47.250 --> 00:05:48.190
They aren't...

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:50.080
backing down!

00:05:52.490 --> 00:05:53.720
This is too dangerous!

00:05:56.820 --> 00:05:58.650
Stop right there, you pack of thugs!

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:14.300
The bicyclist for justice,
Mumen Rider, is here!

00:06:14.610 --> 00:06:16.580
Mumen Rider has come to save us!

00:06:16.610 --> 00:06:18.170
There's nothing to fear if he's here!

00:06:20.210 --> 00:06:22.050
A hero? What a joke!

00:06:22.870 --> 00:06:23.780
Here I go!

00:06:26.890 --> 00:06:28.520
Somebody call an ambulance!

00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:32.680
Mr. Zeniru, you must flee!

00:06:32.680 --> 00:06:37.140
H-Hm. But running away
from terrorists

00:06:37.140 --> 00:06:38.680
would hurt my reputation.

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:40.720
There's no need to leave.

00:06:43.280 --> 00:06:44.850
You're a lucky man,

00:06:45.250 --> 00:06:49.080
having this occur
while I'm still under contract.

00:06:50.610 --> 00:06:52.570
But you're a bodyguard—

00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:53.970
Oh, Sonic!

00:06:54.010 --> 00:06:56.340
Can I leave this to you?

00:06:56.340 --> 00:06:57.570
The men coming are—

00:06:58.470 --> 00:06:59.870
Of course.

00:07:00.660 --> 00:07:03.010
It's their lives you should worry about.

00:07:03.090 --> 00:07:07.480
But please do think of a way to
dispose of the pile of dead bodies.

00:07:08.880 --> 00:07:09.890
The Paradisers...

00:07:10.190 --> 00:07:14.260
A bunch of upstarts equipped with
some new type of battle suit.

00:07:14.850 --> 00:07:17.550
And B-class criminal Hammerhead.

00:07:17.720 --> 00:07:20.060
He might have some backbone.

00:07:20.400 --> 00:07:24.910
THE

00:07:20.400 --> 00:07:24.910
MODERN NINJA

00:07:27.130 --> 00:07:31.350
Boss, you can see Zeniru's building
across the woods.

00:07:31.690 --> 00:07:34.480
People call it the Golden Turd.

00:07:36.320 --> 00:07:37.660
All right, let's go!

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:47.520
Someone's here.{Something's here.}

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:50.730
I've been waiting
for you, Hammerhead.

00:07:52.710 --> 00:07:54.300
Zeniru sent me.

00:07:57.190 --> 00:07:58.800
Let me start out by saying

00:07:59.430 --> 00:08:03.590
No opponent of mine has
ever escaped alive.

00:08:03.900 --> 00:08:05.540
I plan on keeping it that way.

00:08:05.860 --> 00:08:08.030
When it comes to my job,
I'm a perfectionist.

00:08:08.680 --> 00:08:10.440
But if you surrender right now,

00:08:10.440 --> 00:08:11.830
I'll let you live.

00:08:12.990 --> 00:08:15.000
So, what will it be?

00:08:45.100 --> 00:08:46.280
What is this?

00:08:49.570 --> 00:08:50.950
What's going on?

00:08:51.280 --> 00:08:52.310
Why is every—

00:08:57.260 --> 00:08:58.910
Crap!

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:02.520
Bastard!

00:09:10.100 --> 00:09:13.170
What are you trying to do?
Trying to intimidate me?

00:09:13.840 --> 00:09:15.510
You can't see me, can you?

00:09:17.010 --> 00:09:18.560
There you are!

00:09:23.070 --> 00:09:24.460
It's a terrorist!

00:09:24.470 --> 00:09:25.740
No, I'm not!

00:09:32.040 --> 00:09:34.710
So he decided to fight
instead of running.

00:09:44.150 --> 00:09:46.790
Oops, there goes
my bad habit again.

00:09:48.390 --> 00:09:50.920
You're just a little dog bought
by Zeniru's money.

00:09:51.150 --> 00:09:54.390
You think someone like me,
who fights for a noble cause,

00:09:54.390 --> 00:09:57.060
can lose to a dog?!

00:09:57.250 --> 00:09:59.670
Yes, I see what he's up to.

00:09:59.760 --> 00:10:01.790
Just as I thought—
he's a complete fool.

00:10:02.250 --> 00:10:04.040
Couldn't he have at least

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:05.960
tried to arrange the rocks
in a less obvious way?

00:10:08.470 --> 00:10:11.340
There are plenty more rocks
where those came from!

00:10:11.340 --> 00:10:15.160
If you don't stop me,
they'll keep coming.

00:10:15.160 --> 00:10:17.240
So you think you'll be able
to deal with my speed

00:10:17.240 --> 00:10:20.500
if you know which direction
I'm coming from?

00:10:20.910 --> 00:10:23.590
How pathetic.
But I'll play along.

00:10:23.720 --> 00:10:25.000
In fact,

00:10:25.250 --> 00:10:26.340
I'll take you...

00:10:27.030 --> 00:10:27.900
head on!

00:10:34.700 --> 00:10:36.640
He's too fast. I can't see him.

00:10:36.680 --> 00:10:38.800
But it doesn't matter if I can't.

00:10:38.800 --> 00:10:40.020
Because of this!

00:10:42.470 --> 00:10:44.300
Gotcha!

00:10:46.300 --> 00:10:49.150
Think about how stupid
you were to face off against me

00:10:49.150 --> 00:10:51.060
on your way down to Hell!

00:10:55.450 --> 00:10:56.510
It's over.

00:10:56.850 --> 00:10:59.570
Unfortunately,
I couldn't go easy on them.

00:11:00.480 --> 00:11:03.540
Yes, Hammerhead's body is here too.

00:11:03.990 --> 00:11:05.250
I'll head back now—

00:11:07.420 --> 00:11:09.040
The body disappeared?

00:11:12.620 --> 00:11:14.720
That was close!

00:11:14.720 --> 00:11:17.120
Thank goodness he hit my head.

00:11:17.250 --> 00:11:21.560
My skull always was several times
thicker than normal.

00:11:21.950 --> 00:11:24.980
Dammit. I don't know
who that bastard was,

00:11:24.980 --> 00:11:26.190
but one day I'm gonna kill—

00:11:26.320 --> 00:11:26.730
Huh?

00:11:27.410 --> 00:11:29.200
Now who's there?

00:11:35.120 --> 00:11:35.650
Hm?

00:11:37.720 --> 00:11:39.060
Oh, found you.

00:11:52.410 --> 00:11:54.010
As with the mosquito monster,

00:11:54.570 --> 00:11:58.620
I once again underestimated
my opponent's power.

00:11:59.460 --> 00:12:02.500
I let my guard down and Kabuto
took advantage of that.

00:12:03.060 --> 00:12:05.720
If Master Saitama had not been there,

00:12:06.470 --> 00:12:08.700
I would certainly have been destroyed.

00:12:09.480 --> 00:12:10.390
I see.

00:12:10.840 --> 00:12:12.460
Well, I'm glad you're okay—

00:12:12.460 --> 00:12:13.350
Doctor...

00:12:13.840 --> 00:12:16.650
Master Saitama
saved my life twice.

00:12:17.450 --> 00:12:20.090
You, Doctor Kuseno,
restored my life to me.

00:12:20.260 --> 00:12:23.000
Later this same life was saved
by Master Saitama,

00:12:23.270 --> 00:12:25.220
who now has saved it again.

00:12:26.240 --> 00:12:29.100
Yes, I get the picture, Genos.

00:12:29.420 --> 00:12:31.300
What you're trying to tell me is

00:12:31.300 --> 00:12:34.360
how amazing
this Saitama fellow is, right?

00:12:34.400 --> 00:12:34.990
Yes.

00:12:35.910 --> 00:12:39.090
Genos, they're not ready just yet,

00:12:39.090 --> 00:12:41.940
but I am developing
a new series of augmentations.

00:12:42.370 --> 00:12:44.970
When I replace your existing parts
with these new ones,

00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:47.430
you may be able to
surpass this Saitama.

00:12:48.700 --> 00:12:51.400
I imagine he must possess
an enormous amount of strength

00:12:51.480 --> 00:12:54.420
for you go on about him so.

00:12:56.480 --> 00:12:57.150
Yes.

00:12:58.210 --> 00:12:59.590
What's your deal?

00:12:59.640 --> 00:13:01.830
You here to sign up
with the Paradisers?

00:13:01.870 --> 00:13:02.900
No, that's wrong.{ no.}

00:13:03.240 --> 00:13:05.740
I'm just a guy who's a hero for fun.

00:13:06.130 --> 00:13:09.070
For personal reasons,
I'm here to smash your heads in.

00:13:10.220 --> 00:13:12.100
So, where are your followers?

00:13:12.130 --> 00:13:14.110
Then, die!!

00:13:21.160 --> 00:13:23.910
I need to get out of here quickly.{I better get out of here quick.}

00:13:26.530 --> 00:13:27.350
Huh?!

00:13:27.510 --> 00:13:28.840
I thought I punched him?

00:13:30.010 --> 00:13:31.530
What a letdown.

00:13:31.690 --> 00:13:34.850
I was all excited
about these battle suits.

00:13:35.290 --> 00:13:36.980
But the design is lame,

00:13:37.060 --> 00:13:38.730
and all they do is give you
superhuman strength.

00:13:42.510 --> 00:13:44.280
You have no idea how hard it was

00:13:44.420 --> 00:13:46.440
to get hold of these things!

00:13:46.440 --> 00:13:50.380
Bastard, how could you know their value?!

00:13:52.790 --> 00:13:57.960
I've been looking for someone to
test the full power of this suit on!

00:14:06.280 --> 00:14:08.400
Spin attack!

00:14:10.110 --> 00:14:14.320
I used to use that move
all the time when I was a kid...

00:14:16.100 --> 00:14:17.250
Huh?

00:14:18.280 --> 00:14:19.380
No way...

00:14:21.530 --> 00:14:25.410
Hammerhead, huh?
He's a lot like me.

00:14:25.800 --> 00:14:28.650
What the hell are you?!

00:14:37.660 --> 00:14:41.720
W-Wait. I just wanted
to get out of working...

00:14:45.130 --> 00:14:46.790
Don't be bad anymore, okay?

00:14:46.920 --> 00:14:49.690
Huh? So you're
not going to kill me?

00:14:50.180 --> 00:14:52.140
- Get outta here.
- Okay!

00:14:59.660 --> 00:15:01.520
Guess I'll go home.

00:15:03.860 --> 00:15:06.280
Where did Hammerhead go?

00:15:08.920 --> 00:15:10.710
There's no one left but you.

00:15:19.970 --> 00:15:23.040
Hammerhead went that way.
Buck naked.

00:15:26.830 --> 00:15:27.940
What's this?

00:15:34.090 --> 00:15:35.560
Hey, you got it wrong.

00:15:37.110 --> 00:15:38.640
What did I get wrong?{I got what wrong?}

00:15:39.450 --> 00:15:41.900
I'm not their comrade.{I'm not one of the Paradisers}

00:15:43.030 --> 00:15:44.420
You're lying.

00:15:44.460 --> 00:15:47.760
No, no, no.
Don't be dumb—look at me!

00:15:47.760 --> 00:15:49.200
I don't need to.

00:15:49.520 --> 00:15:52.040
With that bald head,
there's no denying it.

00:15:52.680 --> 00:15:53.340
No.

00:15:53.680 --> 00:15:55.460
Look! It's me. Me!

00:15:55.460 --> 00:15:57.680
You know, the guy who's a hero for fun—

00:15:57.680 --> 00:15:58.870
Never heard of you.

00:16:03.470 --> 00:16:05.120
Oh, I see...

00:16:05.120 --> 00:16:07.800
Either way, it doesn't matter.

00:16:08.860 --> 00:16:13.370
You read my attacks. Twice.
That's the real problem.

00:16:14.150 --> 00:16:16.100
Born in a ninja village,

00:16:16.120 --> 00:16:19.420
I've been perfecting
my techniques since childhood.

00:16:20.770 --> 00:16:26.070
Yet you saw right through them.
This I cannot allow.

00:16:27.140 --> 00:16:28.790
What's he talking about?

00:16:29.950 --> 00:16:31.990
My pride won't have it.

00:16:32.310 --> 00:16:36.400
I don't care who you are,
I can't let you simply walk away.

00:16:37.380 --> 00:16:38.490
Oh, come on.

00:16:39.690 --> 00:16:42.610
You just want to try out
your moves on me.

00:16:43.120 --> 00:16:45.570
I can tell by that innocent smile
of yours.

00:16:54.240 --> 00:16:57.660
What do you think of this speed
that beats sound?

00:16:57.790 --> 00:16:59.450
Of these shock waves?

00:17:00.250 --> 00:17:01.450
Can you even see me?

00:17:05.510 --> 00:17:08.020
How can you possibly
keep up with me?

00:17:13.450 --> 00:17:14.630
Can I go home?

00:17:16.100 --> 00:17:17.110
Bastard!

00:17:17.390 --> 00:17:18.970
Wind Blade Kick!

00:17:23.080 --> 00:17:24.270
Checkmate.

00:17:27.620 --> 00:17:29.250
Ah, sorry!

00:17:29.480 --> 00:17:31.640
That wasn't on purpose.

00:17:31.640 --> 00:17:33.230
I meant to stop
before hitting you,

00:17:33.230 --> 00:17:34.990
but your momentum carried
my fist into your...

00:17:38.150 --> 00:17:42.650
WE ARE EXPERIENCING TECHNICAL DIFFICULTIES.
PLEASE STAND BY

00:17:43.190 --> 00:17:46.560
I've worked every job from
assassin to bodyguard.

00:17:46.560 --> 00:17:47.970
I'm the best ninja.{No ninja is more deadly.}

00:17:48.240 --> 00:17:49.650
I am Speed-o'-Sound Sonic!

00:17:50.050 --> 00:17:52.400
But I'm putting my work on hold.

00:17:52.440 --> 00:17:54.990
Now that I've found such
a formidable opponent,

00:17:54.990 --> 00:17:57.470
I'm dedicating myself to training
until we settle this.

00:17:59.180 --> 00:18:00.730
Let me know your name.

00:18:01.440 --> 00:18:02.530
It's Saitama.

00:18:03.190 --> 00:18:04.330
Saitama!

00:18:04.530 --> 00:18:07.280
Next time we meet,
it'll be your demise!

00:18:10.130 --> 00:18:10.710
Okay.

00:18:11.380 --> 00:18:14.090
I, Speed-o'-Sound Sonic,
the ultimate ninja,

00:18:14.320 --> 00:18:16.430
will bring you down without fail!

00:18:17.270 --> 00:18:18.170
Train hard!

00:18:21.290 --> 00:18:23.010
Speed-o'-Sound Sonic?

00:18:23.060 --> 00:18:24.150
Who is that?

00:18:24.330 --> 00:18:27.150
And who would possess such
a redundant name?

00:18:27.410 --> 00:18:28.280
Dunno.

00:18:28.580 --> 00:18:29.700
He suddenly appeared,

00:18:29.700 --> 00:18:31.860
declared we were rivals,
and took off.

00:18:32.000 --> 00:18:34.660
If he is a nuisance,
I will get rid of him.

00:18:34.780 --> 00:18:36.110
Well, you're hardly different.

00:18:36.470 --> 00:18:38.510
Actually, why are you here again?

00:18:38.510 --> 00:18:40.290
Go home.
It's not like we're related.

00:18:40.320 --> 00:18:42.620
Master, I must become stronger—

00:18:42.620 --> 00:18:43.920
Shut up!

00:18:45.500 --> 00:18:50.140
I'm now aware of a serious problem
and am reeling from shock.

00:18:50.320 --> 00:18:52.760
So I beg you, go home for today.

00:18:52.970 --> 00:18:54.270
A serious problem?

00:18:54.850 --> 00:18:58.450
What could cause a problem
for someone as great as you?

00:18:58.660 --> 00:18:59.430
Please tell me.

00:19:07.500 --> 00:19:08.960
No one knows who I am.

00:19:11.860 --> 00:19:15.260
It's been three years since
I first became a hero.

00:19:16.000 --> 00:19:20.370
I've defeated many monsters and
evil organizations during that time.

00:19:20.850 --> 00:19:25.030
I've never heard of any other heroes
doing as much as me.

00:19:25.320 --> 00:19:28.320
Everyone in the world should
know me by now!

00:19:28.600 --> 00:19:32.260
Isn't it weird that I don't have
any fans or anything?!

00:19:32.810 --> 00:19:35.090
You know what he said to me today?

00:19:35.810 --> 00:19:38.580
"Never heard of you."

00:19:38.920 --> 00:19:42.920
Plus, everyone in town took me
for a terrorist.

00:19:43.050 --> 00:19:46.710
They've all forgotten how
I beat those monsters for them!

00:19:47.480 --> 00:19:48.200
He is right.

00:19:48.680 --> 00:19:51.320
The news report did not mention

00:19:51.320 --> 00:19:54.860
m 0 0 l 860 0 860 80 0 80

00:19:51.530 --> 00:19:54.860
Mumen Rider Saves The Day

00:19:51.850 --> 00:19:54.870
Master Saitama or Speed-o'-Sound Sonic.

00:19:55.460 --> 00:19:58.010
Instead, the credit for defeating the Paradisers

00:19:58.020 --> 00:19:59.280
went to a hero called Mumen Rider.

00:20:00.650 --> 00:20:01.440
Wait...

00:20:02.220 --> 00:20:03.000
Master!

00:20:03.850 --> 00:20:06.060
Are you listed with the Hero Registry?

00:20:06.440 --> 00:20:07.580
HERO ASSOCIATION, OFFICIAL HOMEPAGE

00:20:09.020 --> 00:20:12.630
"Take a test at any local branch
of the Hero Association.

00:20:12.630 --> 00:20:14.220
"If you score better than the cut-off,

00:20:14.220 --> 00:20:15.800
you will be registered in
the Hero Registry and

00:20:15.800 --> 00:20:18.920
will be allowed to officially
call yourself a 'hero'."

00:20:18.920 --> 00:20:20.970
"Once you are recognized
by the Association,

00:20:20.970 --> 00:20:22.930
you are deemed a pro and
will get paid

00:20:22.930 --> 00:20:25.720
from donations collected
by the Association."

00:20:26.000 --> 00:20:27.850
"All heroes
in the public eye

00:20:27.850 --> 00:20:31.230
are registered, professional heroes."

00:20:31.410 --> 00:20:33.530
"You may be doing
plenty of hero work,

00:20:33.530 --> 00:20:34.820
but self-proclaimed heroes

00:20:34.820 --> 00:20:36.660
are really just weir...does..."

00:20:36.920 --> 00:20:40.550
"...weirdoes spouting nonsense
viewed with suspicion."

00:20:43.620 --> 00:20:44.920
I had no idea.

00:20:45.490 --> 00:20:47.420
Genos, are you registered?

00:20:47.700 --> 00:20:49.670
No. I feel no need to.

00:20:52.350 --> 00:20:56.690
Let's register! Register with me
and I'll make you my disciple.

00:20:57.230 --> 00:20:58.330
Let's go.

00:21:03.650 --> 00:21:07.140
P-Please... F-Forgive me...

00:21:09.200 --> 00:21:13.070
Pleading for his life after stealing
battle suits from the organization?

00:21:13.210 --> 00:21:15.200
He truly understood nothing.

00:21:15.460 --> 00:21:18.320
Of course,
we did let the theft take place

00:21:18.320 --> 00:21:20.710
in order to collect data from
the suits in the field.

00:21:21.450 --> 00:21:22.420
And the body?

00:21:22.700 --> 00:21:23.590
Leave it.

00:21:25.680 --> 00:21:28.880
Thanks for giving me
my thick skull...

00:21:28.910 --> 00:21:29.940
Mommy.

00:21:30.130 --> 00:21:31.770
I promise I'll get a job!

00:21:32.000 --> 00:21:38.510
APPLICATION FOR HERO TEST

00:21:32.530 --> 00:21:35.400
Our guest today is Mr. Majimeda,

00:21:35.420 --> 00:21:38.510
an expert on the labor issues
confronting young people today.

00:21:38.850 --> 00:21:40.330
Thank you for having me.

00:21:40.390 --> 00:21:42.760
As we saw with
the Paradiser incident recently,

00:21:42.760 --> 00:21:46.630
there's an increase in young people
who lack all motivation to work.

00:21:46.660 --> 00:21:48.640
can you comment on this phenomenon?

00:21:49.660 --> 00:21:52.520
-I'm not so different...

00:21:49.660 --> 00:21:51.850
-Even in the case of the Paradisers,

00:21:51.850 --> 00:21:53.480
I think they've been influenced
by irresponsible lyrics

00:21:53.480 --> 00:21:54.770
in popular songs like
"Don't Give Up on Your Dreams"

00:21:54.770 --> 00:21:55.860
and "Make Your Dreams Come True."

00:21:55.670 --> 00:21:57.090
- ...from those unemployed guys.

00:21:55.860 --> 00:21:58.950
- People who believe such hogwash

00:21:58.950 --> 00:22:05.790
end up making excuses for themselves
and become discouraged.

00:22:05.900 --> 00:22:09.180
One wrong step
and I could've been one of them.

